In some sense, there really isn't a "turning point"... the damage is less
the lower your AC is.  The question is really when something else is more
important than getting another point of AC (for example, with your last
few marker charges, do you want to write EA or something else?)

In practical gameplay, there are a few turning points.

At AC -1, damage starts to be reduced.
At AC -20 to -25, damage reduction is close to saturated.
At AC -40 to -45, monsters start missing a non-trivial amount of time.

So if you're close to AC -40, it's often worthwhile to get a few more
points of AC -- if you can take things from hitting you 80% of the time to
hitting you 40% of the time (which is what 10 points of AC will do for
most monsters in this range), you've effectively doubled your HP again.

So to answer Wes Irby's question, going from AC -36 to -46 causes certain
monsters to miss a lot more often.  They'll still land hits on occasion,
but significantly less often if your AC really drops.

(It should be noted, if you have the patience to play an extinctionist...
even Demogorgon doesn't often hit through AC -128.  In 15 tries, he landed
1 hit on me.  So every point of AC helps!)



